    "created_at": "2020-02-18T19:44:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-18T19:44:04Z",
    "body": "We also have a memory usage module, though I believe it's disabled by default.\r\n\r\nI'm looking into the link provided in the OP, and I think the only other things that might be useful to have is temperatures. Aside from that, I think the other things are either too static to have in the prompt on every draw (e.g # physical CPUs, which is highly unlikely to change), or are simple enough that they can be covered by the custom module system (e.g. other users on the system, which you can get with `$(w | tail +3  |wc)`).\r\n\r\n*Maybe* NIC counters or disk usage could make it in as a module? My inclination would be that that's outside the scope of a shell prompt though.",
