    "created_at": "2020-02-18T19:53:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-18T19:53:45Z",
    "body": "FWIW, apart from those you've already mentioned, Powerlevel10k has the following system-wide prompt segments:\r\n\r\n| Segment | Meaning |\r\n|--------:|---------|\r\n| `vpn_ip` | when on VPN, shows an icon and optionally the IP |\r\n| `ip` | LAN IP address and bandwidth usage (current upload/download speed) |\r\n| `load` | CPU load |\r\n| `disk_usage` | disk usage for the current partition (in percentages) |\r\n| `ram` | free RAM |\r\n| `swap` | used swap |\r\n| `public_ip` | public IP address |\r\n| `proxy` | system-wide http/https/ftp proxy |\r\n| `wifi` | WiFi connection status and speed; optionally lots of other things such as security level and SSID |\r\n\r\nI don't use these myself but I've seen every prompt segment from this list used by someone.\r\n\r\nApart from `public_ip`, everything else shouldn't be hard to implement in Starship. `public_ip` requires network IO, and so cannot be done synchronously while blocking prompt.\r\n\r\nJust some ideas.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
